        "original_id": "2b1d12d2-e93e-54e6-9f06-3ddbe9dea8a0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Newark, Nottinghamshire, England\n- Organizations: UK Parliament, Conservative Party, Standards Committee\n- People: Robert Jenrick, Patrick Mercer\n- Roles: MP, Independent MP\n- Events: 2001 general election, resignation of the parliamentary whip, Patrick Mercer’s resignation, Newark by-election\n\nFacts:\n- Newark is a UK Parliament constituency in Nottinghamshire, England.\n- Patrick Mercer was elected MP for Newark as a Conservative in the 2001 general election.\n- Patrick Mercer resigned the Conservative parliamentary whip in May 2013 following questions about paid advocacy.\n- Patrick Mercer served as an Independent MP for Newark until resigning at the end of April 2014.\n- The Standards Committee suspended Patrick Mercer for six months for a sustained and pervasive breach of the House's rules.\n- Robert Jenrick of the Conservative Party won the Newark by-election on 5 June 2014.\n- Robert Jenrick currently represents Newark in Parliament.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
